{"type":"message","id":"26a9ac90","parentId":"4b92fc9b","timestamp":"2026-06-05T01:19:21.125Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Both TP and SL orders placed successfully:\n- STOP_MARKET BUY @ 1.040 (but I passed 1.0445... Looks like Binance rounded it to 1.040. That might be a tick size issue.)\n- TAKE_PROFIT_MARKET BUY @ 0.983\n\nWait, the SL trigger price is 1.040, not 1.0445 as calculated. This could be Binance's tick size rounding. DOT has 3 decimal precision. But actually if DOT price is around $1, 3 decimal places means 1.044 should work. Let me check...\n\nActually looking at the SOUL.md: \"DOT | 1位\" - DOT has 1 decimal precision. So 1.0445 rounds to 1.0, which is way too low. But the API returned 1.040, which suggests Binance uses 3 decimal places. Maybe the SOUL.md is outdated.\n\nAnyway, the important thing is both orders were placed correctly. Let me verify:","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"DOT 止盈止损已补上。验证一下当前全部干净状态："},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_vaKsNCit6e0TpMJbocPV8861","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd ~/.openclaw/workspace/scripts && python3 -c \"\nimport binance_auto_trade as bat\n\n# 再次确认\nresult = bat.request('GET', '/fapi/v1/openAlgoOrders')\nprint(f'条件委托: {len(result)}单')\nfor r in result:\n    print(f\\\"  {r['symbol']:10s} {r['orderType']:22s} {r['side']:5s} 触发价={r['triggerPrice']:>12s} 数量={r['quantity']:>8s} 状态={r['algoStatus']}\\\")\n\" 2>&1 | grep -v \"InsecureRequest\\|urllib3\\|warnings\"","timeout":10}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":601,"output":666,"cacheRead":47872,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":49139,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780622351365}}
