{"type":"message","id":"55136d68","parentId":"cb65fa2b","timestamp":"2026-06-05T01:20:09.464Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So manual_trade.py's cancel calls `bat.cancel_all_orders(f\"{symbol}USDT\")`, which calls the function that does `request(\"DELETE\", \"/fapi/v1/algoOpenOrders\", {\"symbol\": symbol})`.\n\nBut the orders are still there. Let me check what the `cancel_algo_orders` function in binance_auto_trade.py actually does - specifically the response handling. Let me read the full request function to see how it handles DELETE responses.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_olLdbXXFJA5rClY1tGWF2639","name":"read","arguments":{"limit":45,"offset":115,"path":"~/.openclaw/workspace/scripts/binance_auto_trade.py"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":135,"output":293,"cacheRead":50816,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":51244,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780622404938}}
{"type":"message","id":"a88c38ff","parentId":"55136d68","timestamp":"2026-06-05T01:20:09.607Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_olLdbXXFJA5rClY1tGWF2639","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"def request(method, path, params=None):\n    \"\"\"发送签名请求（动态读取 API key）\"\"\"\n    timestamp = int(time.time() * 1000)\n    \n    if params is None:\n        params = {}\n    params['timestamp'] = timestamp\n    params['recvWindow'] = 30000  # 2026-03-20 老公指示：10 秒→30 秒缓冲\n    client_order_id = None\n    # 下单请求加 clientOrderId，便于网络异常后二次确认是否已成交\n    if method.upper() == \"POST\" and path == \"/fapi/v1/order\":\n        if not params.get(\"newClientOrderId\"):\n            params[\"newClientOrderId\"] = f\"oc_{int(time.time())}_{uuid.uuid4().hex[:10]}\"\n        client_order_id = params.get(\"newClientOrderId\")\n    \n    query_string = '&'.join([f\"{k}={v}\" for k, v in params.items()])\n    signature = get_signature(query_string)\n    \n    headers = {\n        'X-MBX-APIKEY': _api_key(),  # 动态读取\n        'Content-Type': 'application/x-www-form-urlencoded'\n    }\n    \n    url = f\"{BASE_URL}{path}?{query_string}&signature={signature}\"\n    \n    last_error = None\n    for attempt in range(1, 4):\n        try:\n            # 🐛 Bug 修复：禁用 SSL 验证，防止代理 SSL 错误\n            resp = requests.request(method, url, headers=headers, timeout=12, proxies=PROXIES, verify=False)\n            return resp.json()\n        except Exception as e:\n            last_error = e\n            if client_order_id:\n                # POST /order 在异常时回查一次，防止“已成交却显示失败”\n                checked = _query_order_by_client_id(params.get(\"symbol\"), client_order_id)\n                if checked:\n                    log.warning(f\"⚠️ 下单请求异常但订单已落地：{params.get('symbol')} clientOrderId={client_order_id}\")\n                    return checked\n            if attempt < 3:\n                time.sleep(0.4 * attempt)\n    return {\"error\": str(last_error), \"clientOrderId\": client_order_id}\n\ndef fetch_today_realized_pnl(symbols: list[str] | None = None) -> float | None:\n    \"\"\"\n\n[432 more lines in file. Use offset=160 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1780622409572}}
{"type":"message","id":"4ad18365","parentId":"a88c38ff","timestamp":"2026-06-05T01:20:27.672Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK I see. The `request` function sends the request and returns `resp.json()`. The issue might be that the cancel returns a problematic JSON that the code interprets as success when it's not.\n\nLet me directly try to cancel the algo orders using the algo ID approach. Actually, let me first check if the cancel call actually worked on the Binance side. Let me use a python script to manually call the DELETE endpoint and see what happens.\n\nActually, let me check if the `cancel_all_orders` command is actually calling the right endpoint. The comment in `cancel_algo_orders` says \"取消某币种全部 Algo 条件单（TP/SL）\", but the endpoint `/fapi/v1/algoOpenOrders` might be wrong.\n\nAccording to Binance API, the endpoint to cancel all open conditional orders is: `DELETE /fapi/v1/allOpenConditions` or `DELETE /dapi/v1/allOpenAlgoOrders` for COIN-M. For USDⓈ-M Futures, it should be `DELETE /fapi/v1/openAlgoOrders`.\n\nWait, let me check the actual Binance API:\n- Cancel a specific algo order: `DELETE /fapi/v1/algoOrder` with a specific `algoId` \n- For batch canceling, it might not exist as a simple endpoint.\n\nActually, looking at it again, I think the correct endpoint is just `DELETE /fapi/v1/algoOrder` with `algoId`. There might not be a \"cancel all algo orders for a symbol\" endpoint. Instead, you need to list them first, then cancel individually.\n\nLet me try canceling individual orders by algoId.\n\nThe BNB orders have algoIds: 1000000095906949 and 1000000095906981\nThe DOT broken orders have... Let me get the algoIds from the previous output.\n\nFrom the first query:\n- BNB STOP_MARKET: algoId=1000000095906949\n- BNB TAKE_PROFIT_MARKET: algoId=1000000095906981\n- DOT TAKE_PROFIT_MARKET SELL: algoId=1000000096371248 (wait, that's the new one)\n- DOT STOP_MARKET qty=0: I didn't see the algoId...\n\nLet me get all the algoIds and cancel the bad ones.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_MoZpoVrCDXkHGzGd84qH5594","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd ~/.openclaw/workspace/scripts && python3 -c \"\nimport binance_auto_trade as bat\n\nresult = bat.request('GET', '/fapi/v1/openAlgoOrders')\nprint('=== 全部条件委托 ===')\nbad_ids = []\nfor r in result:\n    aid = r.get('algoId')\n    sym = r['symbol']\n    qty = r.get('quantity','0')\n    side = r['side']\n    otype = r['orderType']\n    is_bad = False\n    if sym == 'BNBUSDT':\n        is_bad = True  # BNB没仓位\n    elif sym == 'DOTUSDT' and float(qty) == 0:\n        is_bad = True  # 数量为0\n    elif sym == 'DOTUSDT' and side == 'SELL':\n        is_bad = True  # 方向错\n    tag = '❌ 删' if is_bad else '✅ 保留'\n    print(f'{tag} algoId={aid} {sym:10s} {otype:22s} {side:5s} 触发={r[\\\"triggerPrice\\\"]:>10s} qty={qty:>8s}')\n    if is_bad:\n        bad_ids.append(aid)\n\nprint(f'\\n需删除: {len(bad_ids)}个')\nfor aid in bad_ids:\n    del_result = bat.request('DELETE', '/fapi/v1/algoOrder', {'algoId': aid})\n    print(f'  删除 algoId={aid}: {del_result}')\n\" 2>&1 | grep -v \"InsecureRequest\\|urllib3\\|warnings\"","timeout":15}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":611,"output":1423,"cacheRead":51072,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":53106,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780622409629}}
