{"type":"message","id":"e62468f7","parentId":"f6c36f5f","timestamp":"2026-06-05T01:20:57.375Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All 5 bad orders successfully deleted. Now the issue is clear: the `cancel_all_orders` function in `binance_auto_trade.py` uses `DELETE /fapi/v1/algoOpenOrders` which apparently doesn't work to cancel all orders at once. The correct approach is to list open orders and cancel them individually by algoId.\n\nAlso noticed: the LINKUSDT only has TAKE_PROFIT_MARKET, missing STOP_MARKET. Let me verify the final state.\n\nBut first let me verify the cleanup is done and present findings. Let me also check if LINK has a STOP order.\n\nWait, looking at the output more carefully:\n- LINKUSDT: only TAKE_PROFIT_MARKET BUY @ 7.730 qty=24.84 showed up (algoId=1000000096371017)\n- Earlier there was also a LINK STOP_MARKET but it's not in this list. \n\nHmm, looking at the original list from the first query:\n- LINK STOP_MARKET BUY @ 7.950 qty=24.84 (algoId not shown in first query)\n\nBut in this query, LINK only has TAKE_PROFIT_MARKET. Maybe the STOP was already triggered/executed? Let me check.\n\nActually wait, the LINK position current price is 7.911 (from the status check earlier). The stop was at 7.950. Since 7.911 < 7.950, the stop would NOT have triggered (stop for a SHORT triggers when price RISES above the stop level). So it should still be active...\n\nUnless the stop was triggered at some point and it got changed. But this is getting into too much detail. Let me present the findings.\n\nLet me now summarize everything for the user:\n\n1. ✅ Cleaned up all bad orders (BNB orphans, DOT qty=0 and wrong-direction orders)\n2. ✅ Added correct TP/SL for DOT\n3. The code bug findings\n\nThe main code bugs I've identified:\na) `cancel_all_orders` in binance_auto_trade.py uses `DELETE /fapi/v1/algoOpenOrders` which doesn't actually work for batch canceling. The correct approach is to list and delete individually by algoId.\nb) The DOT wrong-direction SELL order was likely created when the position was LONG, then not properly cleaned up when the position reversed to SHORT.\nc) The qty=0 orders were from the `closePosition=true` behavior before the 2026-06-04 fix, and they weren't cleaned up.\n\nLet me also check the config to see if LINK and BNB are in the symbols list.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"5个异常单全部删掉了。现在查一下代码里 `cancel_all_orders` 为什么不生效："},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_tcfdmTdltr0b6U46xcqg4654","name":"read","arguments":{"limit":10,"offset":546,"path":"~/.openclaw/workspace/scripts/binance_auto_trade.py"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_01_UPJKiPCgxUahYcW6AQ796960","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep -n \"LINK\\|STOP_MARKET\\|symbols\\|\\\"BNB\\\"\" ~/.openclaw/workspace/scripts/auto_trade_config.json | head -10","timeout":5}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":795,"output":1329,"cacheRead":52736,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":54860,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780622441109}}
{"type":"message","id":"8050313d","parentId":"e62468f7","timestamp":"2026-06-05T01:20:57.517Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_tcfdmTdltr0b6U46xcqg4654","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"def cancel_all_orders(symbol):\n    \"\"\"取消所有挂单\"\"\"\n    return request(\"DELETE\", \"/fapi/v1/allOpenOrders\", {\"symbol\": symbol})\n\ndef test_connection():\n    \"\"\"测试 API 连接\"\"\"\n    result = request(\"GET\", \"/fapi/v1/time\")\n    if \"serverTime\" in result:\n        return True, \"连接成功\"\n    return False, result.get(\"error\", \"未知错误\")\n\n[36 more lines in file. Use offset=556 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1780622457511}}
