{"type":"message","id":"b95d91d6","parentId":"6b50b0f9","timestamp":"2026-06-05T06:11:46.666Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK, so the situation has changed:\n\nPositions: 4\n- DOT SHORT -195.7 @ 1.022, floating profit +5.87\n- BNB SHORT -0.33 @ 597.18, floating profit +4.40\n- LINK SHORT -25.38 @ 7.878, floating profit +6.99\n- BTC SHORT -0.003 @ 63200.5, floating profit +2.20\n\nAlgo orders: 7\n- BTC: STOP + TP ✅ (both have qty)\n- LINK: STOP + TP ❌ (both have qty=0!)\n- DOT: only STOP ❌ (no TP! and qty=0!)\n- BNB: STOP + TP ❌ (both have qty=0! and no DOT TP!)\n\nTotal profit: 5.87 + 4.40 + 6.99 + 2.20 = +19.46 USDT\n\nProblems:\n1. LINK STOP + TP both have qty=0 — useless orders\n2. DOT only has STOP, missing TP, and STOP has qty=0\n3. BNB STOP + TP both have qty=0\n\nThis means the `closePosition=true` bug is still happening! The fix from 2026-06-04 was supposed to pass explicit quantity. But looking at these orders, they have qty=0, which means either:\n1. The fix wasn't applied correctly\n2. The place_algo_conditional_order is being called without quantity\n3. Something else is wrong\n\nWait, let me look back at the `place_algo_conditional_order` function:\n\n```python\ndef place_algo_conditional_order(\n    symbol: str,\n    side: str,\n    order_type: str,\n    trigger_price,\n    working_type: str = \"MARK_PRICE\",\n    quantity: float = None,\n):\n    params = {\n        \"algoType\": \"CONDITIONAL\",\n        \"symbol\": symbol,\n        \"side\": side,\n        \"type\": order_type,\n        \"triggerPrice\": format_price(trigger_price),\n        \"workingType\": working_type,\n    }\n    if quantity is not None:\n        sym = symbol.replace(\"USDT\", \"\")\n        params[\"quantity\"] = str(format_quantity(sym, quantity, 0))\n        params[\"reduceOnly\"] = \"true\"\n    else:\n        params[\"closePosition\"] = \"true\"\n    return request(\"POST\", \"/fapi/v1/algoOrder\", params)\n```\n\nSo when quantity is None, it falls through to closePosition=true - which was the old buggy behavior. But the qty=0 orders have `quantity` set to 0 explicitly, not None. The check is `if quantity is not None`, and 0 is not None, so it should use the quantity branch...\n\nWait, but `format_quantity(sym, 0, 0)` returns what? Let me check:\n\n```python\ndef format_quantity(symbol, quantity, price):\n    precision = get_quantity_precision(symbol, price)\n    return int(quantity * 10**precision) / 10**precision\n```\n\nIf quantity=0, then `int(0 * 10**precision) / 10**precision` = `0 / 10**precision` = 0. So `params[\"quantity\"] = \"0.0\"`. This makes sense - quantity 0 is explicitly passed.\n\nBut these orders have quantity 0 in the API response. And they have `closePosition: true` or `false`? Let me check... The reduceOnly field...\n\nActually wait, I didn't print the reduceOnly field in this query. But looking at the earlier queries, when qty=0, it was probably from closePosition=true in the old code.\n\nBut the 2026-06-04 fix was supposed to fix this. Maybe the code wasn't properly saved or the restart didn't pick up the new code? Or maybe somewhere in the code, `place_algo_conditional_order` is still being called without quantity...\n\nLet me check if there are any calls to `place_algo_conditional_order` that don't pass quantity.\n\nLooking at the calls:\n1. `place_order` in binance_auto_trade.py: passes correct tp/sl (line 468, 479) - but these don't pass quantity!\n2. `sync_stop_loss_to_binance`: passes quantity=qty (line 745, 758)\n3. `submit_initial_algo_orders`: passes quantity=qty (line 791, 800)\n\nWait! In `place_order`, the call to `place_algo_conditional_order` at line 468:\n```python\nsl_result = place_algo_conditional_order(\n    symbol, sl_side, \"STOP_MARKET\", formatted_sl\n)\n```\nNo quantity parameter! And at line 479:\n```python\ntp_result = place_algo_conditional_order(\n    symbol, tp_side, \"TAKE_PROFIT_MARKET\", formatted_tp\n)\n```\nAlso no quantity!\n\nThis means `place_order` still calls `place_algo_conditional_order` with `closePosition=true` (because quantity=None). That's the source of the qty=0 bug!\n\nSo the fix in `place_order` was incomplete - the 2026-06-04 fix updated `sync_stop_loss_to_binance` and `submit_initial_algo_orders` to pass quantity, but forgot to update `place_order`!\n\nThe qty=0 orders for LINK, DOT, and BNB show that `place_order` (which creates them during open_position) still uses closePosition=true and gets qty=0 on testnet.\n\nLet me fix `place_order` in binance_auto_trade.py to pass the quantity parameter to `place_algo_conditional_order`.\n\nAlso, DOT is missing TP entirely. Only has STOP with qty=0. This could be because:\n- place_order was called for DOT (open SHORT)\n- TP placement failed or wasn't called\n- Or TP was cancelled and not resubmitted\n\nAnd BNB has STOP + TP with qty=0, which is consistent with place_order using closePosition=true.\n\nSo the fix is: update place_order to pass the formatted_quantity to place_algo_conditional_order.\n\nLet me fix this now.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"有变化，但条件单又出问题了。新开的 DOT / BNB / LINK 的条件单 qty 全是 0。\n\n让我查一下是哪个调用路径没传数量："},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_KH0diUoHNWxIH1kFltXH3459","name":"read","arguments":{"limit":30,"offset":460,"path":"~/.openclaw/workspace/scripts/binance_auto_trade.py"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":462,"output":2821,"cacheRead":75392,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":78675,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780639877416}}
