{"type":"message","id":"6a8bacb6","parentId":"67f3cfa7","timestamp":"2026-06-05T07:03:26.521Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting! The DELETE returned -2011 (Unknown order sent) for both LINK algoIds, but the GET still shows them as active orders. This is exactly the same issue as before - Binance testnet is having consistency problems (orders appear in GET but don't exist for DELETE, creation times out, etc.).\n\nThis is a Binance testnet back-end desync. The orders are in a \"zombie\" state - they show up in the listing but can't be cancelled or modified. They'll probably expire on their own or resolve when Binance fixes their backend.\n\nLet me try one more thing - let me check the BTC orders too (1000000096386969 and 1000000096386980). These were also reported as \"already deleted\" in earlier monitor log, yet they still appear.\n\nThe user opened a new LINK LONG. Now I need to check if monitor is handling the new LINK position properly.\n\nActually, let me focus on what I can help with:\n1. Try to cancel the LINK orphan orders with another attempt (maybe with a different algoId if the GET shows different ones now)\n2. Check if the monitor will create TP/SL for the new LINK LONG\n\nWait, the GET still shows those algoIds. The -2011 means the order doesn't exist on Binance's backend but is still in the listing cache. This is purely a Binance testnet issue.\n\nLet me tell the user: old LINK orders can't be canceled via API either (same -2011 server busy equivalent), this is a Binance testnet zombie order problem. The orders are \"dead\" (0 quantity anyway) and won't trigger. The real issue is the monitor can't create new TP/SL for the new LINK LONG due to -1007 timeouts.\n\nLet me check if the monitor has attempted to create TP/SL for the new LINK LONG.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"和你在 UI 看到的一样 —— API 也删不掉，Binance 返回 `-2011 未知订单`（等同于\"服务器繁忙\"），但查单接口仍显示它们。\n\n这两单是僵尸单：qty=0 不会触发，实际已