{"type":"message","id":"9923b00a","parentId":"368b0c68","timestamp":"2026-06-05T14:49:44.405Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK so there are 7 algo orders for 3 positions (should be 6). Let me analyze:\n\nDOT has 3 algo orders:\n- TAKE_PROFIT_MARKET trig=1.007 qty=206.5 (this is from the OLD DOT closure! It's an orphan from the old DOT LONG @0.9685 with 204.9 qty - wait no, the new DOT has 204.9 amt, and this TP is for 206.5 which is a different quantity)\n- STOP_MARKET trig=0.957 qty=204.9 ✅ (correct for new DOT LONG @0.978)\n- TAKE_PROFIT_MARKET trig=1.010 qty=204.9 ✅ (correct for new DOT LONG @0.978)\n\nSo the TP trig=1.007 qty=206.5 is a leftover from the old DOT LONG that was closed. The manual_trade.py cancel_algo_orders should have cleaned it up, but maybe it only cleaned up 1 of 2 old ones.\n\nActually wait, looking at the close output earlier:\n```\n🗑️ DOTUSDT Algo 单已取消 algoId=1000000096832823\n```\n\nIt only showed 1 cancel. The old DOT LONG had 2 algo orders (STOP and TP). But one was already deleted in a previous cleanup, leaving only 1 to cancel. Then when the new DOT LONG was opened, 2 new orders were created.\n\nBut the old TP (trig=1.007 qty=206.5) is still there. This was from the first DOT LONG @0.9685 that was opened by the monitor and closed manually. The manual_trade close function called cancel_algo_orders which deletes all current orders, but maybe one slipped through?\n\nActually, the qty 206.5 TP at trig 1.007 doesn't match either the old DOT LONG @0.9685 (which had qty ~11.67 with qty=11.7 after format) or the new DOT LONG @0.978 (qty=204.9).\n\nWait, the old DOT LONG had amt=??? from the position query. Let me think: the monitor opened DOT LONG with 20 USDT at 10x = 200 USDT. At entry ~0.9685, qty = 200/0.9685 ≈ 206.5. So the TP order qty=206.5 with trig=1.007 matches the monitor's DOT LONG that I closed.\n\nSo the issue is: the monitor had opened DOT LONG @0.9685 with 206.5 DOT, and created TP orders STOP and TP. When I closed via manual_trade, it cancelled the existing orders, but the new open created 2 fresh orders. And the old TP wasn't cleaned up.\n\nWait, the close showed only 1 algo order cancelled. That means the other one was already gone (maybe the monitor cleaned it). But the TP trig=1.007 qty=206.5 definitely looks like the old DOT position's TP.\n\nActually let me reconsider. The new open created:\n- STOP trig=0.957 qty=204.9\n- TP trig=1.010 qty=204.9\n\nAnd the old remaining from monitor:\n- TP trig=1.007 qty=206.5\n\nThis is exactly 3 DOT orders. One orphan from the monitor's DOT position.\n\nLet me clean it up. The old TP trig=1.007 needs to be deleted.\n\nBut first let me present the state to the user and fix it. ETH and BTC are fine, DOT has an extra orphan TP.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"DOT 调好了，保证金 20 USDT ✅。但多了一单旧 TP 残留，清掉："},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_bCu2SFk5Qxyn4v2MNYcH0219","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd ~/.openclaw/workspace/scripts && timeout 10 python3 -c \"\nimport binance_auto_trade as bat\n# 删 DOT 旧 TP (trig=1.007 qty=206.5，旧仓残留)\nresult = bat.request('GET', '/fapi/v1/openAlgoOrders', {'symbol': 'DOTUSDT'})\nfor r in result:\n    if float(r.get('triggerPrice',0)) == 1.007:\n        aid = r['algoId']\n        bat.request('DELETE', '/fapi/v1/algoOrder', {'algoId': aid})\n        print('已删 algoId=%s (旧DOT TP trig=1.007)' % aid)\n\n# 确认\nresult2 = bat.request('GET', '/fapi/v1/openAlgoOrders')\npos = bat.get_all_positions()\nprint('持仓 %d | 条件单 %d → %s' % (len(pos), len(result2), '✅' if len(pos)*2==len(result2) else '❌'))\n\" 2>&1 | grep -v \"urllib3\\|warnings\"","timeout":15}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":473,"output":1884,"cacheRead":90496,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":92853,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780670961256}}
